title: NyxForge Bounty Lifecycle
---
%%{init: {"fontSize": 18, "theme": "dark", "themeVariables": {"primaryColor": "#1e2030", "primaryTextColor": "#ffffff", "primaryBorderColor": "#5e6ad2", "lineColor": "#a0a8d0", "secondaryColor": "#2a2d3e", "tertiaryColor": "#131421"}, "stateDiagram": {"diagramPadding": 30}}}%%
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> DRAFT : bounty create\n(wizard writes .bounty file)

    DRAFT --> ACTIVE : bounty issue\n(XMR locked on-chain\nDLEQ commitment set)

    ACTIVE --> REDEEMABLE : oracle quorum reached\n(result = met)
    ACTIVE --> EXPIRED : expiry date passes\ngoal not met

    REDEEMABLE --> SETTLED : bounty redeem\n(adaptor + s_met\nXMR swept to holder)

    EXPIRED --> RECLAIMED : oracle publishes s_fail\n(normal path)
    EXPIRED --> RECLAIMED : timelock matures\n(expiry + grace_days)\nno oracle needed

    SETTLED --> [*]
    RECLAIMED --> [*]

    note right of DRAFT
        .bounty file on disk
        collateral not yet locked
        oracles not yet registered
    end note

    note right of ACTIVE
        XMR locked in DLEQ output
        oracles monitoring
        bilateral trading open
    end note
